// `true | true` is a copy, not a case: the second spelling is already covered by
// the first. The duplicate counter compared arms with EACH OTHER, so a repeat
// inside one or-list was invisible to it - and the round that taught the
// coverage reader to walk an or-list moved this cell the wrong way, from
// "refuses with the wrong words" to "accepts".
fn main() { let b: bool = true; match b { true | true => println(1) | false => println(0) } }
